  "prompts": {
    "image": "Generate a NEW photorealistic cinematic 16:9 frame of a quiet railway pedestrian underpass at dusk. Image1 is ONLY geometric blueprint; match camera, man size, opening and stairs exactly. Image2 supplies the actual man's identity and clothing. Image3 supplies authentic grey stone and terrazzo materials ONLY, not architecture. Adult man standing calmly on broad flat corridor floor, seen from behind slightly his left; arms at sides. His LONG damp BROWN HAIR REACHES BOTH SHOULDERS and completely covers his nape. This visible shoulder-length hair silhouette is mandatory, never a short haircut. Charcoal knee-length fine-wool overcoat, pale shirt, dark trousers and shoes, no umbrella. Head at y17%, feet y36%, body x42–46%. Stair landing y50%, opening sides32% and67%, lintel10%. Narrow pilaster behind him. Grey-beige rectangular stone wall panels, medium-grey fine-grained terrazzo floor in large square slabs, same medium-grey terrazzo steps with thin dark anti-slip grooves. Modest warm ceiling pools, soft cool light from entrance, neutral grey balance not orange. Real proportions and solid architecture. One person, no feather, no added props or signage. Single photograph, no low-poly or diagram. Match small person scale of image1; show unmistakably shoulder-length hair even at this size.",
    "endFrameDescription": "Wspólna klatka graniczna f0577; dokładne zakończenie segmentu i początek następnego.",
    "animation": "0-3s: Glide forward down the open staircase toward the stationary listener. Near steps and handrails slide down and outward through parallax as the corridor and listener grow larger. The listener remains planted, arms down, with subtle breathing only. No walking or head turn. Camera motion continues through both boundaries, reaching the supplied End Frame at 3s. Keep architecture rigid and dusk exposure stable. No feather, cuts, dissolves, morphs or new people. @Image1: the existing listener's identity, long hair and coat only; no umbrella or wings. @Image2: station surface materials only, not its viewpoint or signs."
